# Deep-Guard Fix — 2026-07-10T20:03:09+03:30
# File: /tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js  Line: 10  Severity: critical
# Type: sql_injection

## Root Cause
The code concatenates user input directly into the SQL query, allowing for potential SQL injection attacks.

## Explanation
The patch replaces the string concatenation with a parameterized query, which securely binds user input and prevents malicious SQL injection attempts by separating the query structure from the data.

## Patch
--- a/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
+++ b/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
  var query = "SELECT name,id FROM Users WHERE login='" + req.body.login + "'";
-  db.sequelize.query(query, {
+  db.sequelize.query("SELECT name, id FROM Users WHERE login = :login", {
     model: db.User,
     replacements: { login: req.body.login }
   }).then(user => {

